Sometimes a thread must wait until some condition on shared data becomes true: a queue is no longer empty, a flag is set. Polling in a loop wastes CPU. A **`Condvar`** lets a thread sleep until another thread calls `notify_one` or `notify_all`. It is always paired with a `Mutex`:

```rust
let pair = Arc::new((Mutex::new(false), Condvar::new()));
// waiting thread:
let (lock, cvar) = &*pair;
let mut ready = lock.lock().unwrap();
while !*ready {
    ready = cvar.wait(ready).unwrap(); // releases the lock while asleep
}
// notifying thread:
*lock.lock().unwrap() = true;
cvar.notify_one();
```

Channels are built on this mechanism; in application code, a channel is usually simpler.

